# Prettier owns formatting for the JS/TS workspace (docs/coding-standards/typescript.md):
# TypeScript/JavaScript source and the Nx/TS workspace config that goes with it.
# Everything outside that workspace is owned elsewhere and is ignored here so a
# tooling-setup change stays surgical (issue #10):
#   - prose docs (Markdown) are authored by hand, not machine-formatted;
#   - the .NET side (apps/apphost, **/bin, **/obj) is governed by .editorconfig +
#     `dotnet format`, not Prettier;
#   - Spec Kit (.specify/) and specs/ are tool- and human-authored content.

# Build output and caches
dist/
out-tsc/
tmp/
coverage/
.angular/
.nx/

# Dependencies and lockfiles (lockfile format is owned by pnpm)
node_modules/
pnpm-lock.yaml

# .NET side — owned by .editorconfig + dotnet format, not Prettier
apps/apphost/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Generated by the OpenAPI codegen toolchain (ADR-0036): the build-time spec and the typed clients.
# Committed for the CI drift gate, they must match the generator's output exactly, so Prettier must
# not reformat them. Each context's generated-client directory is added as it is created.
apps/identity-api/Roomy.Identity.Api.json
**/data-access/src/lib/generated

# Spec Kit tooling and spec content
.specify/
specs/

# Prose documentation — hand-authored, not machine-formatted
**/*.md

.angular
